---
/**
 * The page GitHub Pages serves for any path that is not in the build.
 *
 * Until this existed a wrong URL produced GitHub's own "Page not found"
 * screen: no branding, no navigation, no way back, and no hint that the site
 * has 52 pages one of which is probably the one you wanted. That screen is
 * what a reader with an old link sees, which is exactly the moment the site
 * has something to offer them.
 *
 * So the search box is the page, not decoration. Pagefind already indexes
 * every built page (`npm run index`) and is embedded on /docs/ the same way;
 * someone who followed a link to a page that moved can type what they
 * remember and find where it went. Everything else here is a fallback for
 * when they would rather browse.
 *
 * One language, deliberately. This file is served for /nonsense and for
 * /it/nonsense alike, because GitHub Pages picks it by status and not by
 * path, so it cannot know which language the reader was reading. It says so
 * and offers both.
 */
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '~/components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '~/components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Page not found — CertMate';
const description =
  'That page is not here. Search the CertMate documentation, the SSL error reference and the deployment guides.';

const card =
  'rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 transition-colors hover:border-primary dark:border-gray-700';
const cardTitle = 'font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white';
const cardText = 'mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} lang="en" noindex>
  <Navbar />

  <main id="main-content" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 px-4 py-16">
    <p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      404
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
      That page is not here
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
      The address may have changed, or the link that brought you here may be
      out of date. The site is searchable, so if you know roughly what you were
      after you can probably find where it went.
    </p>

    <!-- Pagefind, embedded the way /docs/ embeds it: the UI auto-initialises
         against the index built by `npm run index`. Client-side after the
         first load, no third-party service. -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/pagefind/pagefind-ui.css" />
    <div id="search" class="mt-8"></div>
    <script src="/pagefind/pagefind-ui.js" is:inline></script>
    <script is:inline>
      window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
        if (typeof PagefindUI === 'undefined') return; // index not built (dev)
        new PagefindUI({
          element: '#search',
          showSubResults: true,
          resetStyles: false,
          placeholder: 'Search the site',
        });
      });
    </script>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
      Or start from one of these
    </h2>
    <div class="not-prose mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <a href="/" class={card}>
        <span class={cardTitle}>Home</span>
        <p class={cardText}>What CertMate is, and how to install it.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started.html" class={card}>
        <span class={cardTitle}>Documentation</span>
        <p class={cardText}>Setup, DNS providers, storage backends, the API.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/errors/" class={card}>
        <span class={cardTitle}>SSL error reference</span>
        <p class={cardText}>
          What a browser certificate error means, and how to fix it.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href="/deploy/" class={card}>
        <span class={cardTitle}>Deployment guides</span>
        <p class={cardText}>Docker, Kubernetes, nginx, AWS.</p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      Questa pagina è in inglese perché viene servita per qualunque indirizzo
      mancante, in entrambe le lingue, e non può sapere quale stavi leggendo.
      <a href="/it/" class="text-primary hover:underline">Vai alla home in italiano</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
      If a link on this site led you here, that is a bug worth reporting:
      <a
        href="https://github.com/fabriziosalmi/certmate/issues"
        class="text-primary hover:underline">open an issue</a
      >.
    </p>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
